From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: sun6i: wait for FIFO reset completion

Wait for both FIFO resets before programming transfers.
Return a timeout error when reset does not finish.

Adapt Kickpi H618 SDK revision 3ad8e7bd26da.
Use a 1 ms deadline instead of the vendor loop count.

Signed-off-by: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c b/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
@@ -302,6 +303,14 @@
 	/* Reset FIFO */
 	sun6i_spi_write(sspi, SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_REG,
 			SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_RF_RST | SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_TF_RST);
+
+	ret = readl_poll_timeout(sspi->base_addr + SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_REG, reg,
+				 !(reg & (SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_RF_RST |
+					  SUN6I_FIFO_CTL_TF_RST)), 0, 1000);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(&host->dev, "FIFO reset timed out\n");
+		return ret;
+	}
 
 	reg = 0;
 
